From: Auzieman / AuzieTek
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc/85xx: match Tabor's vendor device-tree identity

The retained A-EON tabor3.dts and our shipped tabor-a1222.dtb identify
the machine as varisys,TABOR. The initial forward port accidentally
matched fsl,tabor instead. setup-common.c skips that machine description
and spins indefinitely if no other compatible machine is found.

Preserve the vendor DT identity and correct the machine match. This
restores the identity used by the vendor's former tabor_probe routine.
This source correction alone does not establish hardware boot acceptance.

diff --git a/arch/powerpc/platforms/85xx/tabor.c b/arch/powerpc/platforms/85xx/tabor.c
--- a/arch/powerpc/platforms/85xx/tabor.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/platforms/85xx/tabor.c
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 
 define_machine(tabor) {
 	.name			= "Tabor",
-	.compatible		= "fsl,tabor",
+	.compatible		= "varisys,TABOR",
 	.setup_arch		= tabor_setup_arch,
 	.init_IRQ		= tabor_pic_init,
 #ifdef CONFIG_PCI
